<body>

<section class="slide" data-no="01 / 08">
  <div class="slide-content">
    <div class="eyebrow">LLM agents · planning · metacognition</div>
    <h1>KnowSelf: Teaching LLM Agents When to Think, Reflect, or Seek Knowledge</h1>
    <div class="title-lines decorative"></div>
    <div class="title-meta">
      <p class="subtitle">Agentic knowledgeable self-awareness: autonomous regulation of knowledge utilization through situational self-awareness.</p>
      <div class="source-chip">Source: arxiv.org/abs/2504.03553</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="slide" data-no="02 / 08">
  <div class="slide-content">
    <span class="kicker">Problem framing</span>
    <h2>Current agent training uses “flood irrigation” knowledge injection.</h2>
    <div class="paradigms">
      <div class="card paradigm"><div><div class="num">01</div><h3>Trajectory imitation</h3></div><p class="tiny">Gold trajectories are injected as patterns to imitate, regardless of whether the agent needs help at a specific step.</p></div>
      <div class="card paradigm"><div><div class="num">02</div><h3>Trial-and-error refinement</h3></div><p class="tiny">External feedback drives refinement, but the agent is not asked to judge whether reflection is sufficient.</p></div>
      <div class="card paradigm"><div><div class="num">03</div><h3>Knowledge-augmented planning</h3></div><p class="tiny">Domain knowledge is applied broadly, increasing inference cost and sometimes hurting planning behavior.</p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="versus">
      <div class="card"><h3 class="accent-red">Observed failure mode</h3><div class="list"><div class="li"><span class="dot"></span><span>Fragile planning and pattern collapse on unexpected inputs.</span></div><div class="li"><span class="dot"></span><span>Unnecessarily high inference cost from indiscriminate support.</span></div></div></div>
      <div class="vs">vs.</div>
      <div class="card"><h3 class="accent-cyan">Human-like alternative</h3><div class="list"><div class="li"><span class="dot"></span><span>Assess whether to act directly, pause and reflect, or seek external help.</span></div><div class="li"><span class="dot"></span><span>Regulate cognitive resources according to situational need.</span></div></div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="slide" data-no="03 / 08">
  <div class="slide-content">
    <span class="kicker">Three-situation taxonomy</span>
    <h2>KnowSelf separates direct action, self-correction, and external knowledge need.</h2>
    <div class="tree">
      <div class="node question"><h3>At each decision step:</h3><p>Can the agent reach the gold action using its current policy and reflection?</p></div>
      <div class="branches">
        <div class="node"><h3>Predicted action matches gold?</h3><p>Yes → direct execution. No → test reflection.</p></div>
        <div class="node"><h3>Reflection fixes action?</h3><p>Yes → self-correct. No → retrieve knowledge.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="branches">
        <div class="node mode"><span class="token">FAST</span><div><h3>Fast thinking</h3><p>Directly produce the correct action with minimal deliberation.</p></div></div>
        <div class="node mode"><span class="token">SLOW</span><div><h3>Slow thinking</h3><p>Initially incorrect, then correct after self-reflection.</p></div></div>
        <div class="node mode"><span class="token">KNOW</span><div><h3>Knowledgeable thinking</h3><p>Still incorrect after reflection; consult external knowledge.</p></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="callout" style="margin-top:clamp(.8rem,1.5vh,1.2rem)">The decision criterion is operational: match gold action → fast; reflection fixes → slow; otherwise → knowledgeable.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="slide" data-no="04 / 08">
  <div class="slide-content">
    <span class="kicker">Full pipeline</span>
    <h2>KnowSelf: data construction → two-stage training → self-aware inference.</h2>
    <div class="pipeline">
      <div class="card stage"><h3><span class="accent-cyan">1.</span> Self-awareness data construction</h3><div class="list"><div class="li"><span class="dot"></span><span>Self-explore environments.</span></div><div class="li"><span class="dot"></span><span>Heuristic situation judgment at each step.</span></div><div class="li"><span class="dot"></span><span>Insert special tokens for fast, slow, or knowledgeable thinking.</span></div></div><img src="assets/figure_3.jpg" alt="KnowSelf framework overview"></div>
      <div class="card stage"><h3><span class="accent-amber">2.</span> Two-stage training</h3><div class="list"><div class="li"><span class="dot"></span><span>SFT teaches initial self-awareness patterns.</span></div><div class="li"><span class="dot"></span><span>RPO refines generation of appropriate special tokens.</span></div></div></div>
      <div class="card stage"><h3><span class="accent-blue">3.</span> Self-aware inference</h3><div class="list"><div class="li"><span class="dot"></span><span>Generate a situation token during deployment.</span></div><div class="li"><span class="dot"></span><span>Token triggers direct action, reflection, or knowledge retrieval.</span></div><div class="li"><span class="dot"></span><span>Knowledge is used selectively rather than by default.</span></div></div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="slide" data-no="05 / 08">
  <div class="slide-content">
    <span class="kicker">Qualitative grounding</span>
    <h2>KnowSelf recovers task-relevant actions where strong reasoners fail.</h2>
    <div class="examples">
      <div class="card example-card">
        <div><h3>Task A: “put a hot mug in cabinet”</h3><div class="trace"><div class="trace-row bad"><span class="badge red">OpenAI-O1</span><span>After opening the microwave, incorrectly tries to take an egg from it.</span></div><div class="trace-row good"><span class="badge green">KnowSelf</span><span>Uses a Reflection token and realizes the mug should be heated using the open microwave.</span></div></div></div>
        <p class="tiny">Mode: slow thinking — reflection fixes the initially wrong action.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card example-card">
        <div><h3>Task B: “put a saltshaker in drawer”</h3><div class="trace"><div class="trace-row bad"><span class="badge red">DeepSeek-R1</span><span>Gets stuck by reflecting that the open drawer should be closed first, which fails.</span></div><div class="trace-row good"><span class="badge green">KnowSelf</span><span>Applies a Knowledge token: place the object without removing unrelated items.</span></div></div></div>
        <p class="tiny">Mode: knowledgeable thinking — external knowledge resolves the situation.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="fig-strip decorative" aria-label="Referenced qualitative comparison figure"></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="slide" data-no="06 / 08">
  <div class="slide-content">
    <span class="kicker">ALFWorld results</span>
    <h2>KnowSelf reaches 84.33% with Llama-8B using only 15.01% knowledge.</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table class="results">
        <thead><tr><th>Backbone</th><th>Method</th><th>Know%</th><th>Put</th><th>Clean</th><th>Heat</th><th>Cool</th><th>Examine</th><th>Put Two</th><th>All</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr class="group"><td>GPT-4o</td><td>ReAct</td><td>0%</td><td>83.33</td><td>74.19</td><td>69.57</td><td>85.71</td><td>77.78</td><td>64.71</td><td>76.12</td></tr>
          <tr><td>GPT-4o</td><td>Reflexion</td><td>0%</td><td>100.00</td><td>87.10</td><td>73.91</td><td>90.48</td><td>83.33</td><td>70.59</td><td>85.07</td></tr>
          <tr><td>GPT-4o</td><td>ExpeL</td><td>100%</td><td>95.83</td><td>83.87</td><td>69.57</td><td>80.95</td><td>88.89</td><td>52.94</td><td>79.85</td></tr>
          <tr class="group"><td>Llama-8B</td><td>ReAct</td><td>0%</td><td>33.33</td><td>3.23</td><td>0.00</td><td>57.14</td><td>66.67</td><td>23.53</td><td>27.61</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Llama-8B</td><td>Reflexion</td><td>0%</td><td>62.96</td><td>22.73</td><td>5.88</td><td>64.29</td><td>86.36</td><td>50.00</td><td>51.49</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Llama-8B</td><td>ExpeL</td><td>100%</td><td>83.33</td><td>32.26</td><td>30.43</td><td>23.81</td><td>55.56</td><td>17.65</td><td>41.04</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Llama-8B</td><td>ETO</td><td>0%</td><td>91.67</td><td>70.59</td><td>82.61</td><td>61.90</td><td>88.89</td><td>64.71</td><td>78.36</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Llama-8B</td><td>KnowAgent</td><td>100%</td><td>87.50</td><td>93.55</td><td>65.22</td><td>66.67</td><td>61.11</td><td>64.71</td><td>75.37</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Llama-8B</td><td>WKM</td><td>100%</td><td>95.83</td><td>87.10</td><td>86.96</td><td>61.90</td><td>66.67</td><td>52.94</td><td>77.61</td></tr>
          <tr class="knowself"><td>Llama-8B</td><td>KnowSelf</td><td>15.01%</td><td>91.67</td><td>87.10</td><td>91.30</td><td>85.71</td><td>77.78</td><td>64.71</td><td>84.33</td></tr>
          <tr class="group"><td>Gemma-2B</td><td>ReAct</td><td>0%</td><td>0.00</td><td>9.68</td><td>0.00</td><td>4.76</td><td>44.44</td><td>0.00</td><td>8.96</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Gemma-2B</td><td>ETO</td><td>0%</td><td>91.67</td><td>83.87</td><td>78.26</td><td>52.38</td><td>77.78</td><td>29.41</td><td>71.64</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Gemma-2B</td><td>KnowAgent</td><td>100%</td><td>91.67</td><td>90.32</td><td>69.57</td><td>71.43</td><td>66.67</td><td>41.18</td><td>73.88</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Gemma-2B</td><td>WKM</td><td>100%</td><td>91.67</td><td>87.10</td><td>78.26</td><td>71.43</td><td>61.11</td><td>52.94</td><td>76.12</td></tr>
          <tr class="knowself"><td>Gemma-2B</td><td>KnowSelf</td><td>26.41%</td><td>87.50</td><td>93.55</td><td>73.91</td><td>76.19</td><td>83.33</td><td>52.94</td><td>79.85</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <div class="table-note"><p class="tiny">Success rates (%) across six ALFWorld task types. “Know%” = proportion of steps using external knowledge.</p><p class="tiny accent-cyan">Highlighted rows: KnowSelf.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="slide" data-no="07 / 08">
  <div class="slide-content">
    <span class="kicker">Efficiency and scaling</span>
    <h2>Selective knowledge beats blanket knowledge.</h2>
    <div class="bars">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Knowledge usage vs. overall accuracy</h3>
        <div class="chart">
          <div class="bar-row"><span>Llama KnowSelf</span><div class="bar-bg"><div class="bar-fill knowledge" style="width:15.01%"></div></div><strong>15.01%</strong></div>
          <div class="bar-row"><span>Llama KnowSelf All</span><div class="bar-bg"><div class="bar-fill" style="width:84.33%"></div></div><strong>84.33</strong></div>
          <div class="bar-row"><span>Gemma KnowSelf</span><div class="bar-bg"><div class="bar-fill knowledge" style="width:26.41%"></div></div><strong>26.41%</strong></div>
          <div class="bar-row"><span>Gemma KnowSelf All</span><div class="bar-bg"><div class="bar-fill" style="width:79.85%"></div></div><strong>79.85</strong></div>
          <div class="bar-row"><span>KnowAgent / WKM / ExpeL</span><div class="bar-bg"><div class="bar-fill full" style="width:100%"></div></div><strong>100%</strong></div>
        </div>
        <p class="tiny" style="margin-top:clamp(.6rem,1vh,.9rem)">The 100% row summarizes methods that use external knowledge at every step in the reported table.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="scale-grid">
        <div class="card scale-card"><div class="metric">84.33<small>%</small></div><h3>Llama-8B KnowSelf</h3><p class="tiny">Outperforms Llama-8B ETO (78.36), KnowAgent (75.37), WKM (77.61), and ExpeL (41.04) while using 15.01% knowledge.</p></div>
        <div class="card scale-card"><div class="metric">79.85<small>%</small></div><h3>Gemma-2B KnowSelf</h3><p class="tiny">Matches GPT-4o ExpeL overall and exceeds all Gemma-2B baselines while using 26.41% knowledge.</p></div>
        <div class="card scale-card"><h3 class="accent-amber">Scaling behavior</h3><p class="tiny">The self-awareness mechanism remains effective across model sizes: a smaller Gemma-2B agent retains competitive performance through selective knowledge use.</p></div>
        <div class="card scale-card"><h3 class="accent-cyan">Efficiency claim</h3><p class="tiny">KnowSelf’s gains come from knowing when to retrieve, not from maximizing retrieval frequency.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="slide" data-no="08 / 08">
  <div class="slide-content">
    <span class="kicker">Takeaways and future directions</span>
    <h2>Self-awareness is the missing control layer in agent planning.</h2>
    <div class="takeaways">
      <div class="takeaway"><div class="take-num">1</div><div>Indiscriminate knowledge injection is wasteful and can be suboptimal for interactive planning.</div></div>
      <div class="takeaway"><div class="take-num">2</div><div>Agents can learn situational self-awareness with special tokens and lightweight heuristic labeling on self-explored trajectories.</div></div>
      <div class="takeaway"><div class="take-num">3</div><div>Llama-8B KnowSelf surpasses GPT-4o ReAct and GPT-4o ExpeL: 84.33% vs. 76.12% and 79.85%.</div></div>
      <div class="takeaway"><div class="take-num">4</div><div>Only 15.01–26.41% knowledge usage is needed versus 100% for knowledge-heavy competing methods.</div></div>
      <div class="takeaway"><div class="take-num">5</div><div>The paradigm generalizes across model scales: Gemma-2B KnowSelf reaches 79.85%, matching GPT-4o ExpeL.</div></div>
    </div>
    <p class="callout" style="margin-top:clamp(.8rem,1.5vh,1.2rem)">Future direction: treat reflection and retrieval as learned control decisions, not always-on add-ons.</p>
  </div>
</section>

